## TICKET 3 — EI: Table 1 must show the FULL composition, all strengths (`ei_core.py`)

**Bug.** Table 1 renders only the selected worst-case strength under a "For 100 mg" banner, dropping the 50 mg and 25 mg columns; the extractor picks the largest-value amount column for the CALCULATION and displays only that.

**Fix (display-only; no math change).** Mirror `residual_solvent._build_display_columns` ("Table 1 shows the composition as uploaded — including EVERY strength column; only the calculation is restricted to the one selected column"). In `parse_composition_excel` / `_ei_finish_composition` and the template path `_TPL.ei_osd_result`: keep ALL detected quantity/strength columns in `columns`/`_display_columns` and every row's full `columns` map verbatim (100/50/25 mg, material code, function, vendor — every column the sheet has); remove the "For {N} mg" single-strength banner; show strengths side by side; never sum/merge/average across strengths in the display. The worst-case selection feeds ONLY `calculate_ei_tables`, never Table 1. Single-strength products unaffected.

**Expected.** Table 1 is a faithful copy of the uploaded Excel with all strength columns present; calculation tables unchanged.

