## TICKET 7 — RS: material-name fallback must never default to the API/product name (`residual_solvent.py` / `residual_solvent_annexure_converter.py`)

**Bug.** RS Section 9 shows a truncated "Magnesium" (unmatched, supplier "-") though the LIGAMED negative declaration is uploaded; and three annexures (CEOLUS/Asahi, both Opadry) were labelled "Sitagliptin phosphate monohydrate". When the vendor material name can't be parsed, extraction falls back to the request's product/API name and/or truncates.

**Fix.** The material-name fallback ladder must be: document body → extractor candidates → document title → filename-derived name (`_rs_filename_derived_name`) → "Material [N]". It must NEVER fall back to the product/API name, and must not truncate a name to a single word. Same class as the DEG/EG "raw filename as name" fix. Product-agnostic.

**Expected.** Magnesium stearate → full name, mapped to the LIGAMED declaration (all-NA, correct); CEOLUS and both Opadry annexures show their real vendor identities, not the API name.

