## TICKET 8 — RS: coating-variant-per-strength + duplicate annexure (`residual_solvent.py`)

**Bug (a).** For the assessed 100 mg strength (Opadry Brown, 12 mg) the tables also render Opadry Yellow (50 mg variant) as a "q.s." row and drop Orange (25 mg). **Bug (b).** MCC appears twice — Annexure 3 (IFF, covering MCC + Croscarmellose) and Annexure 4 (Asahi CEOLUS) — a duplicate from the many-to-many mapping over-firing.

**Fix.** (a) For the selected strength, a composition variant whose quantity is NA/blank at that strength is NOT part of the formulation — exclude it entirely from the tables (never render it, never as q.s.). Only the variant present at the selected strength (Brown at 100 mg) is assessed. (b) When two annexures legitimately cover the same material, map that material to ONE (prefer the material-specific CoA over a multi-material PRDS, else the higher-confidence identity); do not emit two annexure rows for one composition material. Product-agnostic; keep the many-to-many mapping for genuinely distinct materials (MCC + Croscarmellose from one IFF doc stays correct).

**Expected.** 100 mg tables show only Opadry Brown; Yellow/Orange absent (not q.s.); MCC maps to a single annexure.

