## Cross-cutting
Tickets 1, 4, 5 are the SAME provenance principle (a regulatory/guideline number is a reference, never the material's content) applied in three places — the pattern that fixed Aerosil/Sitagliptin-API and then broke Trila/Vaso when done by value. Ticket 2 is its mirror (a stated `<X` bound IS the material's evidence and must be kept). Ticket 3 is the display twin (copy the source faithfully; restrict only the calculation). Tickets 6/7/8 are identity/mapping fidelity. No per-product logic; nothing inspects a value against a constant.

